.TH "MATHMLELEMENT.NONCE" "3JS" "June 17, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MathMLElement.nonce \- MathMLElement: nonce property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]nonce\f[B]\f[R] property of the \f[CR]MathMLElement\f[R]
interface returns the nonce that is used by Content Security Policy to
determine whether a given fetch will be allowed to proceed.
.SH VALUE
A String; the cryptographic nonce, or an empty string if no nonce is
set.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Retrieving a nonce value
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] math = document.querySelector(\(dqmath\(dq);
console.log(math.nonce);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]HTMLElement.nonce\f[R] a similar property for HTML elements.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]SVGElement.nonce\f[R] a similar property for SVG elements.
